            9. Who Should Skip It
          </h2>

          <p>
            Skip FlavCity if protein per dollar is your priority. At roughly $3 to $4 per serving, it costs two to three times as much per gram as a plain grass-fed whey, and part of its protein is collagen. Anyone drinking a shake every day will feel that difference in their monthly grocery bill quickly.
          </p>

          <p>
            Skip it if you are a drug-tested athlete or need lab-verified purity. With no third-party testing claims and no published certificates of analysis, there is nothing for you to check. A certified isolate, or a brand that publishes batch results, is the safer choice, and our <a href="/naked-nutrition-protein-powder-review/">Naked Nutrition review</a> covers a cheaper grass-fed alternative.
          </p>

          <p>
            Skip it if you want to buy on Amazon. We could not confirm an official FlavCity listing on Amazon US, and buying food supplements from unknown third-party sellers carries real risks around storage and authenticity. If Amazon is where you shop, the alternatives on this page are the better route.
          </p>

          <p>
            And check allergens carefully. The dairy smoothies contain milk; the PB&amp;J flavors contain peanuts; the plant-based vanilla contains almond; and coconut milk powder appears across the range. Anyone with a milk, peanut or tree nut allergy needs to read each flavor's label. People with kidney disease should get a protein target from their doctor before adding any protein powder.
          </p>
        </div>

