          <p>
            <strong>For a breakfast smoothie:</strong> this is what FlavCity is designed for. Shake one serving with 12 oz of milk, which also adds about 8 g of complete protein and offsets the collagen share, or blend it with ice and frozen fruit. The packets are handy for travel and the office, where blending is not an option.
          </p>

          <p>
            <strong>For muscle building:</strong> FlavCity is not the efficient choice. If you do use it after training, make it with milk or add a second protein source so you reach a full dose of complete protein. A plain whey isolate or concentrate does the job for less money. <strong>For dairy-free buyers:</strong> the Plant-Based Vanilla works, but a pea-based blend usually gives more protein for less.
          </p>

          <p>
            <strong>The cheaper homemade version:</strong> one serving of unflavored grass-fed whey, half a frozen banana, a spoon of cocoa or cinnamon, a splash of coconut milk and a few drops of stevia gets you close to FlavCity's chocolate smoothie for well under half the price. Compare other real-ingredient brands in our <a href="/truvani-protein-powder-review/">Truvani review</a>.
